[Desktop Entry]
# herdr, in a terminal window of its own (tiled, not a popup: it is where you work, beside
# an editor, and a popup would close at the first click elsewhere; dwl gives it its tile's
# size). Closing the window only detaches: the agents keep working in herdr's background
# server, and the next start shows them again where they were. Its own app-id (kawa-agents)
# and title ("Agents", then "Agents · <workspace>" as herdr sets it); it starts in ~/repos,
# where your projects are (theme.sh makes the folder) — herdr's first workspace is the
# folder it was started in. Its icon: our seal of 代 (the launcher draws it: X-Fedokawaii-Kanji).
Type=Application
Name=Agents
GenericName=Coding agents side by side
Comment=herdr: Claude Code sessions in panes, each marked working, blocked or idle
X-Fedokawaii-Kanji=代
Exec=footclient -N -a kawa-agents -T Agents -D @HOME@/repos -- herdr
Terminal=false
Categories=Development;
Keywords=herdr;claude;agents;ai;worktree;
